# 201 · A paused or closed run's judge jobs stop holding up the rest

**Status:** `VERIFIED` · **Version:** [v0.2.2](../../roadmap.md#v02x)

## What

From [issue 50](https://github.com/iammrduncan/thermite/issues/50), the field report's fifth request, as it applies to v0.2.1. Each item was checked against the code on 2026-11-10; goal [202](../202-field-report-3080.goal) holds the check of every item of the report.

The judge never takes a paused run's queued jobs: its lease takes only a running run's (`harness/ledger/jobs.ts`, "A paused or closed run's jobs wait in the queue"). Three other places count those jobs as work under way, and wait for work that can't start until the run is resumed:

1. **A lane's development run on a shared device.** It waits while the judge has a job queued or leased (`harness/agents/devrun.ts`, `judgeBusy`, which counts every run's jobs). So a running run's lanes can't run `run_experiment` for as long as another run is paused with jobs queued: each trial gives up when it ends, with no experiment run. It counts only the jobs the judge can take: a running run's, and leased ones. Sharing a device says today that paused runs' jobs hold the lanes; that line changes with it.
2. **The judge's hold on a shared runner.** On a runner the judge shares with the lanes, the judge holds the runner for a step whenever a job is open (`harness/judge/judge.ts`, `tick`), a paused run's included, then finds nothing to take, while the lanes wait for the runner. It holds the runner only when a job it can take waits.
3. **Terminate on a RunPod rig.** Terminate pauses the rig's runs, then waits until no judge job is queued or leased, at most an hour, and then refuses (`control/runpod/lifecycle.ts`, `quiescing`). The runs it paused keep their queued jobs, which never start, so with any queued at that moment the pod bills for the hour and is not terminated. It waits for the jobs that run: the leased ones. This was found by reading the code while checking the report: a test shows it before the fix.

A closed run's queued jobs are cancelled, but control is not told:

4. **A closed run's cancelled jobs are recorded.** Closing a run cancels its queued jobs (`harness/ledger/jobs.ts`, `endClosedRuns`) without a `job_cancelled` event, the event a cancel by the owner writes. Control builds its view of the judge's queue from events, so it shows them queued for good: the rig's page (`with N queued`), the run's **Judge queue**, `get_run`'s `judge_waits` and the operator's brief. Steer a run says the rig's page no longer counts them as queued, which is not true yet. Each cancelled job gets its event.

## Why

In the report, one old queued job stalled a new campaign on an idle GPU. The same count can keep a run's lanes from any experiment, keep a pod billing for an hour without the terminate the owner asked for, and show the owner work that will never run.

## Done when

- [x] Items 1 to 4, each with a test that fails without its fix.
- [x] The acceptance checks the changes touch: agents (item 1), runners (item 2), RunPod (item 3) and control (item 4).
- [x] Pages: Sharing a device, Steer a run, the RunPod rig's Terminate, and the changelog.

## Decisions

- 2026-11-09, the owner: v0.2.0 ships what was built ("cut v0.2.0 with what changes we have now"), and each fix after it is a version of its own; this goal is a fix, and moves to v0.2.x.
- 2026-11-10, the owner: v0.2.2 fixes critical bugs only ("Fix only critical bugs, not user experience changes. The v0.3.0 will change a lot of user experience bits."). This goal is v0.2.2's, with items 1 to 4. Its former items that change how a run behaves for the owner leave it, and goal 202 records where they go: pause and close stop the judge's job at its next block (today the judge finishes it, as Steer a run says), Resume asks before it pauses another run on the rig, and lanes may work beside the judge's calibration on a shared device.

## Progress

- 2026-11-03: Goal written for v0.1.3's plan, from the open issues of its milestone.
- 2026-11-10: Rewritten for v0.2.2 from a check of the report against v0.2.1 (`main` at 0d984fb7). Item 3 is new: found while checking the report's paused-run items.
- 2026-11-10 06:58 UTC: verified on `patch/v0.2.2`. Item 4 (ad574882), items 1 and 2 (fb948f17), item 3 (7dd7073b), each with a test that failed before its fix: the close-run tests, the dev-runs test and `tests/harness/ledger/jobs-open.test.ts`, the RunPod terminate test. Item 3's test confirmed the bug before the fix. The agents (27/27), runners (11/11), RunPod (28/28) and control (17/17) acceptance checks passed, and the full `npm run check`. Ships in v0.2.2.

